        "node_id": "n_9_2fb238",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 is incorrect because it assumes the optimal set is always a prefix of the sorted probabilities, which fails when a single high-probability friend (e.g., 0.8) is better than including lower-probability friends that increase the chance of getting more than one problem; the correct approach is to sort probabilities in descending order and iteratively add friends only if their inclusion increases the probability of getting exactly one problem.",
